      "math_academy_id": "q-335654",
      "sequence_position": 12,
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=8x(1-0.75x)-xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-4y+4xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ Evaluating the Jacobian of the system at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[1,\\,2]^{T},$ we get\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$J({x}^{∗})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"40px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"40px\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$\\,.$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix are \n{{field-5}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}$ is \n{{field-6}}{{field-7}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote ${f}_{1}(x,y)=8x(1-0.75x)-xy$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=-4y+4xy.$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8x(1-0.75x)-xy)=8-12x-y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(8x(1-0.75x)-xy)=-x \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-4y+4xy)=4y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-4y+4xy)=-4+4x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the Jacobian matrix is\n\n$$\nJ=[\\begin{aligned}8-12x-y & -x \\\\ 4y & -4+4x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\nJ({x}^{∗})=[\\begin{aligned}8-12(1)-(2) & -(1) \\\\ 4(2) & -4+4(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix, we write down the characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-6-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 8 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-6-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-8(-1) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation, we get the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2\\text{ and }{\\lambda }_{2}=-4.$ Since both eigenvalues are real and negative, our equilibrium is $\\text{an asymptotically stable}$ $\\text{sink}.$",
